# What must never reach a build context.
#
# Not only for size — though that matters, since the context is uploaded to the
# daemon on every build and `node_modules` alone is several hundred megabytes.
# The first three entries are the ones that matter for safety: a `.env` copied
# into an image is a credential in a layer, readable by anyone who can pull it,
# and `docker history` will show it even after a later layer deletes the file.

.env
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

.git
.github
.serena
.claude
.cursor

node_modules
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/dist
**/target

# Screenshots and test output.
shots
till-shots
e2e/shots

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp

# Documentation and specifications do not run.
docs
zatca-docs
*.md
!README.md
